@startuml
title UML sequence - Implemented simulated outgoing submission (WP-21)
actor Customer
actor Operator
actor Checker
participant "Browser / BFF" as API
participant "Payments worker" as Pay
participant "Current controls / Identity" as Gates
participant "Core" as Core
database "Payments store" as Store
participant "Synthetic rail provider" as Rail
database "Simulator store" as ProviderDB
Customer -> API : Verified SIMULATED recipient; exact quote; action reauthentication; confirmation
API -> Store : Save original accepted intent before scheduling
Pay -> Store : Lock original intent, recipient and current rail policy
Pay -> Gates : Current ownership, restrictions, proof and signed checks
alt Paused / denied / expired before possible submission
 Pay -> Core : Release only a bound, unsubmitted reservation if present
 Pay -> Store : Record paused or nonexecution outcome
else Current gates allow
 Pay -> Core : Reserve exact principal + fee and gross daily budget
 Core -> Core : Payer lock; expiry / product / pricing / funds / budget checks
 Core --> Pay : Immutable reservation authority and active hold
 Pay -> Store : Stage stable provider instruction
 Pay -> Core : Mark bound hold submitted before any possible HTTP effect
 Pay -> Store : Persist attempt marker + fenced, short lease
 Pay -> Store : Commit before network call
 Pay -> Rail : Signed original instruction (bounded HTTP)
 Rail -> ProviderDB : Deduplicate identity + digest; persist acceptance + immutable evidence
 alt Accepted but response lost
  Rail --x Pay : Timeout after provider commit
  Pay -> Store : OUTCOME_UNKNOWN; retain submitted Core hold
 else Authenticated acknowledgement
  Rail --> Pay : Signed ACCEPTED / PENDING evidence
  Pay -> Store : Receipt + SUBMITTED (pending); no booked payment
 end
end
Operator -> API : Pause new submissions
API -> Store : Current role; serialize policy revision; pause immediately
Pay -> Store : Recover original durable work / expired lease
Pay -> Rail : Signed inquiry of original identity, also while paused
Rail -> ProviderDB : Retrieve original instruction and immutable current evidence
Rail --> Pay : Signed matching evidence / NOT_FOUND observation
Pay -> Store : Recheck fence after locks; save current pending / reconciliation status
note over Pay,Core
Unknown outcome and NOT_FOUND never release submitted funds.
Provider acknowledgement does not establish settlement.
Final evidence proceeds through the independent Core booking/release path.
end note
Operator -> API : Propose resume bound to exact policy and revision
Checker -> Gates : Independent canonical person approves exact proposal
Operator -> API : Apply approved resume
API -> Gates : Current maker and checker authority; exact approval digest
API -> Store : Recheck current revision; resume only new submissions
@enduml
